# Format is the following:
# LCN
# list of sentences, one per line
# label: lower_prob <= P(phi) <= upper_prob for Type 1
# label: lower_prob <= P(phi|psi) <= upper_prob for Type 2
# IMPORTANT: pay attention to spaces between
# also, the empty lines and the ones starting with # are skipped
#
# 7-variable example LCN from docs/scc_factor_graph.tex (SCC Factor-Graph Propagation).
# Propositions: A, B, C, D, E, X, Y
# Structure-graph edges: X->A, Y->B, A->B, B->C, C->D, D->B, C->E
# The constraints c_BC, c_CD, c_DB form a directed cycle B->C->D->B,
# so Tarjan's algorithm yields one non-trivial SCC S_BCD = {B, C, D}.
# Condensation DAG: S_X -> S_A -> S_BCD, S_Y -> S_BCD, S_BCD -> S_E.
#
# Exact marginals (verified against the 128-world global NLP):
#   P(A)=[0.42,0.94] P(B)=[0.21,0.82] P(C)=[0.3333,0.8571]
#   P(D)=[0.1333,0.8667] P(E)=[0.50,0.70] P(X)=[0.60,0.80] P(Y)=[0.30,0.50]

c_X1:  0.6 <= P(X1 | U1) <= 0.8
c_X2:  0.3 <= P(X2 | X3 and X1) <= 0.5
c_X3: 0.7 <= P(X3 | X2 and X1) <= 0.9
c_X4: 0.2 <= P(X4 | U4) <= 0.4
c_X5: 0.5 <= P(X5 | U5) <= 0.7
c_X6: 0.6 <= P(X6 | X2 and X4 and X1 and X7) <= 0.8
c_X7: 0.4 <= P(X7 | X2 and X4 and X5 and X6) <= 0.6
c_U1: 0.3 <= P(U1) <= 0.5
c_U4: 0.1 <= P(U4) <= 0.3
c_U5:  0.5 <= P(U5) <= 0.7

